257 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 184 0 R
/E (The increasing interconnectedness of the modern world has facilitated unprecedented economic growth, international mobility and technological innovation. However, these same developments have also enabled organised criminal groups to expand their operations across national borders. Among the most profitable forms of transnational organised crime are human trafficking and migrant smuggling, crimes that exploit vulnerable populations while generating billions of dollars in illegal revenue annually. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
258 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 184 0 R
/E (Although often discussed together, human trafficking and migrant smuggling represent distinct criminal activities governed by separate legal frameworks and requiring different law )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
259 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 184 0 R
/E (One of INTERPOL's most recognised tools is its Notice System. Notices serve as )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
260 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 184 0 R
/E (international requests for cooperation rather than legally binding warrants. The most well-known, the Red Notice, requests member countries to locate and provisionally arrest a wanted individual pending extradition, surrender or similar legal action. Other notices )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
261 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 184 0 R
/E (facilitate locating missing persons, identifying unidentified bodies, warning member states about dangerous criminals, sharing criminal methodologies and tracing wanted individuals. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
262 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 184 0 R
/E (INTERPOL also manages one of the world's most comprehensive criminal information systems through its secure global communication platform, I-24/7. This system enables law enforcement agencies to rapidly access databases containing fingerprints, DNA profiles, travel documents, stolen vehicles, firearms, works of art, organised crime intelligence and notices relating to international fugitives. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
263 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 184 0 R
/E (Within the context of human trafficking and migrant smuggling, INTERPOL's )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
264 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 184 0 R
/E (responsibilities include coordinating multinational operations, facilitating intelligence exchange, identifying trafficking networks, supporting victim identification, enhancing border security cooperation and providing specialised training for national police services. While the organisation cannot independently arrest traffickers or prosecute offenders, its ability to )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
265 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 184 0 R
/E (connect law enforcement agencies across jurisdictions makes it indispensable in dismantling transnational criminal organisations. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
266 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 184 0 R
/E ( Introduction to the Agenda )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
