269 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 185 0 R
/E (enforcement responses. Human trafficking is fundamentally a crime against individuals, involving exploitation through force, coercion, deception or abuse of vulnerability. Migrant smuggling, in contrast, primarily concerns the facilitation of illegal entry into a country for financial or material benefit. Nevertheless, the two crimes frequently overlap in practice, with migrants initially smuggled across borders later becoming victims of trafficking. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
270 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 185 0 R
/E (Numerous global developments have intensified these challenges in recent decades. Armed conflicts, political instability, poverty, climate-induced displacement, economic inequality and restrictive migration policies have increased the number of individuals seeking irregular migration routes. Organised criminal groups have exploited these circumstances by establishing sophisticated international networks capable of recruiting victims online, forging travel documents, laundering illicit profits through complex financial systems and coordinating activities across multiple jurisdictions. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
271 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 185 0 R
/E (Technological advancements have further transformed these criminal enterprises. Social media platforms, encrypted messaging applications, cryptocurrencies and dark web marketplaces have enabled traffickers and smugglers to recruit victims, advertise illegal services, coordinate )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
272 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 185 0 R
/E (logistics and evade law enforcement with increasing sophistication. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
273 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 185 0 R
/E (Given the transnational nature of these crimes, no single country can effectively combat them )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
274 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 185 0 R
/E (in isolation. Success depends upon timely intelligence sharing, coordinated investigations, harmonised legal frameworks, efficient extradition procedures and sustained operational cooperation between national law enforcement agencies. As the primary international platform for police cooperation, INTERPOL occupies a central position in facilitating these efforts. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
275 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 185 0 R
/E (Delegates must therefore examine not only how individual states can strengthen domestic responses but also how the international law enforcement community can enhance collective action while respecting national sovereignty, human rights and existing international legal obligations. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
276 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 185 0 R
/E (The International Criminal Police Organization \(INTERPOL\) exists to facilitate international police cooperation while respecting the sovereignty and domestic laws of its member countries. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
