/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 190 0 R
/E (domestic legislation, inconsistent investigative capacities, corruption, limited resources and varying evidentiary standards frequently hinder effective international cooperation. Criminal organisations exploit these weaknesses by relocating operations to jurisdictions with weaker enforcement capabilities or limited international coordination. )
