417 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 196 0 R
/E (In addressing this agenda, nations should focus on practical measures that strengthen international cooperation while remaining within INTERPOL's mandate. Discussions should emphasize improving coordination between national law enforcement agencies to prevent, investigate, and dismantle transnational trafficking and migrant smuggling networks. Key areas for deliberation include enhancing intelligence sharing through INTERPOL's communication systems, strengthening joint cross border investigations, improving border security while protecting the rights of migrants and trafficking victims, and using emerging technologies to detect and disrupt criminal activities. As trafficking and migrant smuggling continue to evolve, delegates should consider innovative, collaborative, and victim centred approaches that enhance international police cooperation while respecting national sovereignty, human rights, and international law. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
